# <Project> Agent Instructions

<!-- Copy to <repo>/AGENTS.md. Target size: ≤ 6 KB — it is loaded on every
     session in this repo. Over 10 KB, go looking for content that belongs at
     another layer (see ../README.md, "The placement test").

     ONE RULE ABOVE ALL: this file holds what an agent CANNOT infer from the
     codebase and CANNOT read from config. Everything else is somewhere better.
     -->

<One paragraph: what this system is, what it runs on, and what the system of
record is. Enough that an agent reading only this knows what it is touching.
Name the things that are NOT true too, when they are the obvious wrong guess —
"Slack is an outbound integration, not the record", "this is Web Deploy, not a
container deployment". Those sentences prevent more wasted work than any
amount of architecture description.>

## Start here

- Read `README.md` and `.planning/PROJECT.md` for product context.
- Read `.planning/STATE.md` and `.planning/ROADMAP.md` for current work.
- Inspect `package.json` / the solution file for current commands. **Do not
  copy changing stack or milestone state into this file** — it goes stale and
  then it lies.
- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes and keep narrow work narrow.

## Running it locally

```text
<install command>
<dev server command>
<test command>
<lint / typecheck command>
```

<Anything non-obvious about running it: a service that must be up first, a
port that is not the default, a build step people forget.>

## Milestone close — repo-specific inputs

<!-- The ritual itself lives in gsd-settings.md §6 and runs unattended. Do NOT
     restate the gates here. What the ritual cannot know is below, and if any
     of it is missing the agent has to stop and ask — which is the whole thing
     this section exists to prevent. -->

| | |
|---|---|
| **Base branch** | `<main \| dev>` |
| **Environments** | `<dev → test → prod, or "single environment">` |
| **Deploy command** | `<per environment>` |
| **Watch the deploy** | `<how to follow it to a terminal state — log command, status URL, or CI run>` |
| **Deployed URL** | `<one per environment — the agent loads these in a browser after deploying>` |
| **Test / UAT command** | `<command>` |
| **Tag scheme** | `<e.g. vMAJOR.MINOR, annotated, on the base branch>` |
| **Rollback** | `<command or procedure>` |

## Safety rules specific to this repo

<Only genuinely repo-specific hazards. Each one should name a concrete thing
that breaks. Examples of the right shape:

- Never clobber runtime-managed rows from seed or migration scripts; `<script>`
  may create missing bootstrap rows, but existing `<Table>` rows must survive.
- Production schema changes are forward-only through `<command>`.
- Tests must not read or write the production database.
- `<shared resource>` is high-blast-radius — changing it affects `<other systems>`.

If a rule would be true of every repo we own, it belongs in `global-prompt.md`,
not here.>

## Domain vocabulary

<Terms that mean something specific here and would be misread otherwise. Skip
this section if there are none — an empty section is worse than no section.>

## Sources of truth

- `README.md`, `.planning/PROJECT.md` — product and architecture
- `.planning/STATE.md`, `.planning/ROADMAP.md` — current work
- `.planning/config.json` — GSD behavior (read it; never restate it here)
- `<package.json / *.sln>` — commands
- `<cloudbuild.yaml / .github/workflows/>` — deployment
- `<schema file>` — data model

